"If traffic increases from 1,000 to 100,000 requests/sec, I would first put an API Gateway and Load Balancer in front of the services. I would use horizontal scaling to increase the number of service instances and distribute traffic across them.

I would apply rate limiting to protect the system from overload. For read-heavy GET requests, I would use caching to reduce database load. Wherever immediate response is not required, I would use asynchronous processing with Kafka.

I would also scale the database using techniques such as read replicas, connection pooling, and appropriate partitioning/sharding where required. Finally, I would implement backpressure so that when downstream services cannot handle the traffic, the system slows or buffers requests instead of crashing."

